From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: do not require NSS when S/MIME is disabled

FindSMIME.cmake searches for NSPR and NSS and stops the configure when it
cannot find them, regardless of ENABLE_SMIME:

  CMake Error at cmake/modules/FindSMIME.cmake:76 (message):
    NSPR headers not found.  Use -DWITH_NSPR_INCLUDES=/path/to/nspr to
    specify the include dir of NSPR.

even though the build passed -DENABLE_SMIME=OFF. The module's own header
says it should not: "Searches for Mozilla's NSS and NSPR libraries, unless
-DENABLE_SMIME=OFF is used". ENABLE_SMIME appears exactly once in the file,
declaring the option, and is then never tested.

It goes unnoticed wherever something else has already put NSPR in the
sysroot, which is why this only shows up on a tree built from scratch: the
same configuration succeeded on a long-lived one that happened to carry
nspr from an earlier build, and failed on a fresh one.

Guard the search with the option the file documents. The three variables
the module exports are set before the guard, so consumers still see them
defined and empty when S/MIME is off.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/cmake/modules/FindSMIME.cmake
+++ b/cmake/modules/FindSMIME.cmake
@@ -26,6 +26,12 @@
 set(mozilla_nss "")
 set(MOZILLA_NSS_LIB_DIR "")
 
+# Everything below looks for NSPR and NSS and calls FATAL_ERROR when it does
+# not find them, whether or not S/MIME was asked for. The header of this file
+# says otherwise - "unless -DENABLE_SMIME=OFF is used" - and that is the
+# behaviour restored here.
+if(ENABLE_SMIME)
+
 # Use pkg-config when none is specified
 if((WITH_NSPR_INCLUDES STREQUAL "") AND (WITH_NSPR_LIBS STREQUAL "") AND (WITH_NSS_INCLUDES STREQUAL "") AND (WITH_NSS_LIBS STREQUAL ""))
 	foreach(pkg nspr mozilla-nspr firefox-nspr xulrunner-nspr seamonkey-nspr)
@@ -154,3 +160,5 @@
 if(MOZILLA_NSS_LIB_DIR STREQUAL "")
 	set(MOZILLA_NSS_LIB_DIR "${LIB_INSTALL_DIR}")
 endif(MOZILLA_NSS_LIB_DIR STREQUAL "")
+
+endif(ENABLE_SMIME)
